7. Claims

Definition 7.1 (Claim). With a private constructor,

\mathrm{Claim}(cs, T, \alpha) := \bigl\langle \mathrm{cid} : \mathbb{N},\ \mathrm{proof} : \mathrm{Proof}(cs, T),\ \mathrm{verifier} : \mathrm{Verifier},\ \mathrm{ctx} : \mathrm{Context},\ \mathrm{authBound} : \alpha \le \mathrm{verifier}.\mathrm{auth},\ \mathrm{inTheta} : \mathrm{verifier}.\mathrm{id} \in \mathrm{ctx}.\mathrm{caps} \bigr\rangle.

The invariants authBound and inTheta are fields of the type. Any Claim value satisfies them, whether or not it was produced by sealClaim. This is the correction to v10.0's Theorem 5.1, which was true by signature alone.

Definition 7.2 (SEAL).

\frac{
\begin{array}{c}
p : \mathrm{Proof}(cs, T) \quad w : \mathrm{Witness} \quad \mathrm{Compat}(H, p, w) \\
v : \mathrm{Verifier} \quad v.\mathrm{id} \in \mathrm{ctx}.\mathrm{caps} \quad \alpha \le v.\mathrm{auth} \\
r : \mathrm{Reform}(P, T) \quad r.\mathrm{formalizerId} \ne \mathrm{producer}
\end{array}
}{
\mathrm{sealClaim}(H, \mathrm{ctx}, \mathrm{cid}, \mathrm{producer}, v, \alpha, p, w, r) : \mathrm{Claim}(cs, T, \alpha)
}

Theorem 7.3 (Claim soundness, mechanized). A claim c : \mathrm{Claim}(cs, T, \alpha) satisfies T under the assumption that some checker in cs is sound:

\bigl(\exists k \in cs.\ \mathrm{Sound}(k)\bigr) \Rightarrow T.

```lean
theorem Claim.sound {cs : List Checker} {T : Prop} {α : Authority}
    (c : Claim cs T α) (hs : ∃ k, k ∈ cs ∧ Sound k) : T := c.proof.sound hs
```

Theorem 7.4 (Ancestor bound, mechanized). For any claim c, \alpha \le x for every ancestor x of c.\mathrm{verifier}:

\forall x \in c.\mathrm{verifier}.\mathrm{lineage}.\ \alpha \le x.

