9. Architecture

9.1 Layers

Layer Component Interface Trust boundary
1 Ontology (Eigenius/EigenTT) Claim cs T α multi-checker TCB + axiom whitelist
2 Execution (EviBound) Candidate → Artifact → VerifiedArtifact runner-side signing (§9.4)
3 Capability (Cerise/Cerisier) Capability[α], versioned points-to Cerisier memory model
4 Freshness (NISTIR 8213 draft v2) Attest(claim, pulse) \exists i.\ \mathrm{Beacon}_i honest

9.2 Operational Semantics

\mathrm{Claim} \xrightarrow{\text{Approval}} \mathrm{Candidate} \xrightarrow{\text{Exec}} \mathrm{Artifact} \xrightarrow{\text{Verify}} \mathrm{SealedClaim}

9.3 Cerisier Boundary

Cerisier is used for host/memory hardening: unforgeable capabilities, sentry capabilities, version-numbered points-to, local enclave attestation. Credential-DAG revocation is a separate epoch-based mechanism (§8).

9.4 Runner-Side Signing (Corrected)

v10.0 signed after the fact with sk_\alpha. Version 11.0 requires the runner to sign the provenance record before releasing the artifact:

\mathrm{Attestation} = \mathrm{Sign}_{sk_\text{runner}}\bigl(\mathrm{Hash}(T) \parallel \mathrm{run\_id} \parallel \mathrm{artifact\_hashes} \parallel \mathrm{SLSA\_provenance} \parallel \mathrm{sealedAt}\bigr).

The verifier's signature is a second signature binding the runner's attestation to an authority; the runner signature is what prevents retrospective artifact substitution.

9.5 Corrected CVE Scope

CVE-2026-69146 affects MLflow 3.13.0–3.15.0: LogInputs is absent from BEFORE_REQUEST_HANDLERS, allowing any authenticated user to inject DatasetInput records into another user's lineage via POST /api/2.0/mlflow/runs/log-inputs. It does not substitute run_ids or touch artifacts or metrics. The architectural lesson is unchanged: cryptographic provenance binding replaces a mutable tracking server as the root of trust.

