10. Separation Constraint

Design Constraint 10.1. Anchor consistency (V_0, \mathcal{M}, \mathcal{R}) cannot be certified from within the claim layer.

Justification. Self-certification of anchors requires the system to reason about its own consistency (Gödel II). Formalisation sketch: type the constitutional set in a universe \mathcal{U}_\text{const} and show that no total function \mathcal{U}_\text{const} \to \mathrm{Prop} can certify its own soundness without external stipulation. Status: design constraint, not mechanized.

Corollary 10.2. Anchor consistency is constitutional and logged externally.

