Appendix C — Architecture Specification

C.1 Layer Model

```
   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │ L4  Freshness       NISTIR 8213 draft v2 beacon combination │
   │     Attest(claim, pulse) → SignedAttestation                │
   ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
   │ L3  Capability      Cerisier (PLDI 2026)                    │
   │     Capability[α], versioned points-to, sentry caps         │
   ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
   │ L2  Execution       EviBound / MLflow + provenance binding  │
   │     Candidate → Artifact → VerifiedArtifact                 │
   ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
   │ L1  Ontology        Eigenius / EigenTT                     │
   │     Claim cs T α, Proof cs T, Witness, Reform               │
   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Interfaces. Each layer exposes a typed boundary:

Layer Provides Requires
L1 Claim cs T α, sealClaim, promote Proof cs T from L2, Capability[α] from L3
L2 VerifiedArtifact, in-toto attestation Runner key sk_runner
L3 Unforgeable capability tokens Host isolation
L4 Freshness nonces Beacon public keys

C.2 Message Formats

VerifiedArtifact (L2 → L1).

```
message VerifiedArtifact {
  string  run_id;
  bytes   artifact_hash;      // SHA-256 of artifact bytes
  bytes   provenance;         // DSSE-wrapped SLSA predicate
  bytes   runner_signature;   // Sign_{sk_runner}(...)
  uint64  sealed_at;          // ledger timestamp
}
```

Attestation (L4 → L1).

```
message Attestation {
  uint64  epoch;
  bytes   beacon_output;      // SHA-512 combination per §2.3
  bytes   precommitment;      // SHA-512(local_random)
  bytes   verifier_signature; // Sign_{sk_α}(...)
}
```

C.3 Configuration Invariants

· I1 (Checker non-empty). Every Proof cs T satisfies cs ≠ [] by the nonempty field.
· I2 (Hash domain separation). H used in Compat is domain-separated from any other hash use; enforced at the L2/L1 boundary.
· I3 (Provenance monotonicity). L.deps is append-only; no entry is removed once written.
· I4 (Signer permanence). L.signer c is fixed at sealing and never rewritten.
· I5 (Effective-time monotone). For a fixed verifier, rev(v) is either none or some t; if some t, no later reassignment occurs.

