7. Ledger, HOLD, and Transitive Taint

```
   LEDGER L
   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │  deps     : Nat → List Nat     (claim c depends on these)   │
   │  signer   : Nat → Nat          (verifier that sealed c)     │
   │  sealedAt : Nat → Nat          (timestamp of sealing)       │
   └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   DEPENDENCY GRAPH  (arrows point from dependent → dependency)

        c4 ────► c3 ────► c2 ────► c1 ────► c0
        │        │        │        │
        │        │        │        └── sealed by v1
        │        │        └── sealed by v2
        │        └── sealed by v2
        └── sealed by v3

   REVOCATIONS  rev : Nat → Option Nat
        rev(v1) = some t1     (compromise time t1)
        rev(v2) = none
        rev(v3) = none

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   HOLD (least predicate closed under H-direct and H-taint)

     H-direct:   rev(signer c) = some t  ∧  t ≤ sealedAt c
                 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
                                 Hold c

     H-taint:    d ∈ deps c   ∧   Hold d
                 ──────────────────────────
                            Hold c

   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   PROPAGATION (assume sealedAt c0 < t1, others ≥ t1)

        HOLD c0    ←   direct (sealed before compromise, survives)
        HOLD c1    ←   direct (sealed after compromise, held)
        HOLD c2    ←   taint via c1
        HOLD c3    ←   taint via c2
        HOLD c4    ←   taint via c3

   THEOREM 8.5 (hold_of_depStar):
        DepStar L c d  ∧  Hold L rev d   ⟹   Hold L rev c
